# Start here on Android

**Screen 06 — Crest the Rinse Arch. The Codex structural experiment was rejected for promotion.**

Open **Review_on_Android.pdf** for the full comparison in order. Each of its 29 pages contains one complete picture. To zoom into individual pixels, use the original files included alongside the PDF.

1. **APPROVED.jpg** is the owner's exact original image. Its original GitHub path is **references/06_crest_the_rinse_arch.png**. The bytes and resolution are identical.
2. **CLAUDIA_BEFORE/opening.png** is the retained playable Screen 06 from **claude/rainbow-s06-match-c17** at **c649fcbc35780e11cefce83eb54684f1d55752a5**.
3. **CODEX_NEW/opening.png** is the rejected structural game build from **codex/s06-world-space-rinse-arch** at game source **a1c1f0c7e35239c9f7065a56f19b79264313994c**.
4. **CLAUDIA_BEFORE/ride.mp4** and **CODEX_NEW/ride.mp4** show genuine uninterrupted Three.js swims using the same course, steering, camera and clock. The clip covers the full Screen 06 inlet to the Screen 07 transition. It runs 5.25 seconds at 12 fps. The simulation ran at 60 steps per second.
5. **diagnostics/visible-crest-and-swim.png** is an annotated copy of the original. Orange marks the established route. Cyan follows the original crest's photographed coins at inferred surface depths. Its legend describes the study.

All native pictures are 864 × 1536. Each of the two game folders contains 14 matched PNGs. Open the same basename in each folder to compare a pose.

